// Alert query (DIAAT-285): client-side errors in transcribe-web in the alert window, by
// error type and where it was caught. Used by the "ui-errors" alert (measure: failures).
//
// Source (browser, DIAAT-205, replacing browser Sentry; transcribe-web
// lib/browser-failures.ts, relayed by transcribe-api's POST /api/telemetry): "ui.error",
// from the error page (ui.error_source "render", with the Next.js digest that links it
// to the server error) and the window's handlers ("window_error",
// "unhandled_rejection"). ui.error_type is the error's class name (TypeError,
// ChunkLoadError), never its message or stack.
// Area: both. Pages of both areas send it and relayed browser events carry no area.
// Caveats: each page sends one event per type, source and route a minute, and at most
// 20, so a tight error loop counts as a few events, not thousands. A lower bound: a
// page that crashes before its batch is sent loses it. ChunkLoadError after a release
// (an old page asking for removed scripts) is expected for a few minutes.
// Output (AC3): error_type, source (ui.error_source) and a count. No route or digest.
customEvents
| where name == "ui.error"
| extend error_type = tostring(customDimensions["ui.error_type"]),
    source = tostring(customDimensions["ui.error_source"])
| summarize failures = sum(itemCount) by error_type, source
| project error_type, source, failures
